    "description": "The CLIVAR Moored Instrument Data Assembly Centre is located at BODC and was\nestablished in 2004. BODC has responsibility to acquire, quality control,\narchive and deliver the moored instrument data collected during CLIVAR. The DAC\ndeals with moored time series data in delayed mode, rather than data from real\ntime observing systems. The data are mainly from current meters and ADCPs,\nthough other types of moored instrument such as microcats and thermistor chains\nare also handled.\n\nData from different international projects associated with CLIVAR are collated\nat BODC and converted to a common NetCDF format. Data are currently available\non request and will later be made available online.",
